		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1742#p1742"><![CDATA[
Well, it took almost 2 months of prodding, but DevMaster.net finally added the Blender Game Engine to their Game Engine database. If you aren't aware of this already, the DevMaster list is the most complete list of commercial and opensource game engines on the internet. Here's the Blender community's opportunity to let everyone know just how great Blender's Game engine really is!!!<br><br>Please visit the site (direct link found below) and post a review. The results of the reviews are tabulated for the database rating system.<br><br><a href="http://www.devmaster.net/engines/engine_details.php?id=347" class="postlink">http://www.devmaster.net/engines/engine ... php?id=347</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=424">bigkahuna</a> — Sat Sep 16, 2006 2:36 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
